---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const proseClass = 'prose prose-neutral max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif-jp prose-headings:text-shrine-ink prose-a:text-shrine-vermillion';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy" description="How this site handles personal information and data.">
  <section class="bg-shrine-indigo-dark py-14 text-shrine-paper">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6">
      <h1 class="font-serif-jp text-2xl font-bold sm:text-3xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-shrine-paper/75">
        How this site handles personal information and data.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
    <div class={proseClass}>
      <p>
        Shrine The Pantheon ("this site") respects the privacy of its visitors and is committed to handling personal information responsibly. This page explains how information is handled on this site.
      </p>

      <h2>1. About the Operator</h2>
      <p>
        This site is operated by an individual. Please use the <a href="/en/contact/">contact page</a> to reach the operator.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Analytics (Google Analytics)</h2>
      <p>
        This site uses Google Analytics (GA4), a web analytics tool provided by Google, to help improve the site. Google Analytics uses cookies to collect traffic data, which is gathered anonymously and does not identify you personally. You can opt out by disabling cookies in your browser settings. For details on how this data is collected and processed, see <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's policies and terms page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Embedded Third-Party Content</h2>
      <p>
        This site embeds Google Maps for location information and YouTube videos for visiting guidance. Some shrine pages may also display posts from an official X (formerly Twitter) account. The providers of these services may collect information via cookies or similar technologies. Please refer to each provider's own privacy policy for details.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Affiliate Programs</h2>
      <p>
        The "Nearby Accommodation" section on each shrine page links to search results on Booking.com and (on Japanese pages) Rakuten Travel. This site may participate in these companies' affiliate programs in the future, in which case the linked partner may use cookies or similar technologies via third-party ad services to collect visitor information.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Contact Form</h2>
      <p>
        Contact inquiries are handled through a Google Form. Any information you provide (such as your name or email address) is used only to respond to your inquiry. Please also see <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a> for how Google Forms handles data.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Data Stored in Your Browser (Favorites &amp; Visit History)</h2>
      <p>
        The "Favorites" and "Mark as Visited" features store data in your browser's local storage only — nothing is sent to a server. This data will not carry over if you switch browsers or devices.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        We make every effort to keep the shrine information on this site (history, access, visiting hours, goshuin availability, etc.) accurate, but we cannot guarantee its accuracy or completeness. Visiting hours and goshuin availability in particular can change, so please check each shrine's official information for the latest details. The operator is not responsible for any damages arising from the use of this site.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        This site may update this policy without prior notice, to the extent permitted by law. Any changes take effect as soon as they are posted on this page.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about this policy, please reach out via the <a href="/en/contact/">contact page</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="text-sm text-shrine-ink-soft">Effective date: August 17, 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
